'' NO OVERLOAD TAKES A UDT WHOSE CASTS ARE 'byref as const wstring' AND 'any ptr' at a
'' 'const wstring ptr' parameter -- sys/win's BSTRING passed to tkMsg. fbc-modern says error
'' 99, "No matching overloaded function", for the classic program. The report was kept quiet
'' for any UDT with an 'operator cast', so the call stayed untyped and the build stopped on
'' TKO0994, "this statement was not compiled", once per call.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i tests/modules/src/castovl/libs tests/modules/src/castovl/app/bad.tiko -o tests/modules/castovlbad.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: bad.tiko(5,17): error TKO0632: no overload of 'count' matches these arguments
'' EXPECT-OUT: bad.tiko(6,17): error TKO0632: no overload of 'count' matches these arguments
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0994
'' EXPECT-NO-FILE: tests/modules/castovlbad.exe
